WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:04.033
-Our next guest is a filmmaker
whose new documentary series

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:06.601
"Unprecedented" is streaming on
Discovery+.

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:07.834
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.067
-The shot is beautiful, sir.

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:19.133
-Okay.

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:23.601
Can we get the orange out,
please?

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:26.701
Is that possible?
It's very orangey.

00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:28.934
I don't know why that is.

00:00:28.934 --> 00:00:32.601
-Please welcome to the show
Alex Holder, everybody.

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:34.467
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:44.234
♪♪

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:45.868
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:49.367
-It's a pleasure.
-So, you have made a few

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:52.934
documentary films before,
and then you made this series,

00:00:52.934 --> 00:00:56.501
which is -- Basically, you were
with the Trump family,

00:00:56.501 --> 00:00:58.300
the Trump campaign
before the election

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.901
all the way up to January 6th.
-Yeah.

00:00:59.901 --> 00:01:02.567
-And I think one of the things
people have been taken with,

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:05.200
who have watched this, is
the amount of access you got

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:06.801
to the Trump family.

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:11.234
Why do you think it is that they
agreed to it, and what were

00:01:11.234 --> 00:01:13.834
the secrets you used to get them
to make that decision?

00:01:13.834 --> 00:01:16.000
-I mean, so I was originally
introduced to them,

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.701
and then I think they were
really confident

00:01:19.701 --> 00:01:21.200
they were going to win
the election.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:25.534
So here was a guy with a funny
accent that was going to

00:01:25.534 --> 00:01:28.033
showcase them winning
the 2020 election.

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:30.767
Also, I didn't really have any
skin in the game politically,

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:33.501
so why not, here's a guy
going to film us.

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:36.901
I don't think they planned
the inevitable outcome,

00:01:36.901 --> 00:01:39.434
at least I didn't expect it,
so yeah.

00:01:39.434 --> 00:01:42.033
-And you got to film in
the White House, obviously.

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:44.100
What was it like?

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.901
I would imagine no matter who
the president is, there are

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:49.033
some stresses involved with
going and setting up

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:50.434
a film shoot in the White House.

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:52.801
-So, it was a remarkable
experience.

00:01:52.801 --> 00:01:55.167
I mean, to go inside, we take
out all the equipment,

00:01:55.167 --> 00:01:57.968
the dogs come out, sniff
everything, eventually we go

00:01:57.968 --> 00:02:00.434
inside to the residence
of the White House.

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:02.367
This is the diplomatic reception
room.

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:06.968
And none of the crew had ever
really filmed

00:02:06.968 --> 00:02:08.734
in the White House before.

00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:11.000
And so we didn't know what
the protocol was.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.901
So, there's a few White House
ushers that are inside,

00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:15.400
and I start talking to
one of them.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.934
In the middle of the
conversation, he just stops

00:02:17.934 --> 00:02:20.934
talking and he looked like he
was about to have a stroke.

00:02:20.934 --> 00:02:22.634
I mean, literally,
his eyes popped out.

00:02:22.634 --> 00:02:24.634
It was just, like,
suspended animation.

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:26.467
So I was like,
"What's going on?"

00:02:26.467 --> 00:02:28.934
And, basically, Michael,
my director of photography,

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:33.200
had moved a chair, and the guy
was like mouthing wordlessly,

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:36.400
like -- like, "You literally
can't do this,"

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.033
and eventually he managed to get
his words together.

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:41.868
And Michael -- he goes,
"You can't move that chair."

00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:44.167
So Michael actually puts the
chair back, and he's like,

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:46.167
"No, no, no,
stop moving the chair.

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:48.334
That chair is
Abraham Lincoln's chair.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.767
I mean,
it was absolutely insane.

00:02:50.767 --> 00:02:52.801
I mean, just completely mad.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:54.601
-Well, that's Lincoln's fault
for leaving it there.

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:55.834
-Exactly. Right. Exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:57.968
-You know, at some point,
you know?

00:02:57.968 --> 00:02:59.434
I'm pretty sure
he has his own bedroom.

00:02:59.434 --> 00:03:00.501
They could put it in there.

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:01.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.701 --> 00:03:03.767
So, one of the things
that happened

00:03:03.767 --> 00:03:06.067
that must have been surreal
for you -- I imagine many steps

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:09.701
of this were surreal --
but the January 6th committee

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:14.133
subpoenaed your film, like you
had interviews that, you know,

00:03:14.133 --> 00:03:18.234
reflected different people's
state of mind about January 6th.

00:03:18.234 --> 00:03:21.901
And because it was subpoenaed,
and because it turned up there,

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.868
you've been accused of
being a spy,

00:03:23.868 --> 00:03:27.634
that you had sort of implanted
yourself in the campaign

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:29.167
for the purposes of this.

00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:31.367
One, what was it like getting
subpoenaed in the first place?

00:03:31.367 --> 00:03:33.167
And two, how have you reacted to

00:03:33.167 --> 00:03:35.300
some of the conspiracy theories
about your involvement?

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:36.934
-I think I'm definitely
the first spy

00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:38.334
ever to be on this show,
I think.

00:03:38.334 --> 00:03:39.934
-Yeah.
-It's not exactly good --

00:03:39.934 --> 00:03:42.934
-Well, I'll say this, you're
the first one who's admitted it.

00:03:42.934 --> 00:03:45.367
[ Laughter ]
-Exactly. Exactly.
Exactly. Exactly.

00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:47.734
No, I mean, the whole thing
has been completely surreal.

00:03:47.734 --> 00:03:50.601
I mean, when you get the e-mail
with the subpoena attached that

00:03:50.601 --> 00:03:54.133
says, you know, "Alex Holder,
you're hereby commanded to

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.000
appear, you know, in
the United States

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.968
House of Representatives,"
I mean, obviously it's a pretty,

00:03:58.968 --> 00:04:00.834
you know, surreal experience.

00:04:00.834 --> 00:04:04.868
And I think when I actually went
into the hearing and --

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:06.400
So, it's in a private room.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:07.634
It's the same room that you see

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:10.634
on all the January 6th clips
they show.

00:04:10.634 --> 00:04:12.300
And I was sort of pulling
the chair back,

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:14.901
and I was thinking like, "What
the [bleep] is going on?

00:04:14.901 --> 00:04:16.267
I mean, this is absolutely
crazy.

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:19.200
I mean, honestly,
like it's just mad."

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.834
And then, yeah, I mean, I think
all the conspiracy theories that

00:04:22.834 --> 00:04:25.400
have come out have also
been somewhat strange.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:28.501
I'm an MI6 spy
and I'm an undercover FBI agent.

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:30.767
-Right.
-So, you know, I'm both sides.

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:32.501
-You wear a couple of
different hats,

00:04:32.501 --> 00:04:35.834
and that's what everybody
respects about you as a spy.

00:04:35.834 --> 00:04:37.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.367 --> 00:04:39.467
Very few people can do both.

00:04:39.467 --> 00:04:43.501
The clip we showed where
the former president comes in

00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:45.534
and he's very taken
with the floors --

00:04:45.534 --> 00:04:47.434
He says, "Look at these floors."

00:04:47.434 --> 00:04:51.067
That's at Mar-a-Lago,
so those are his floors.

00:04:51.067 --> 00:04:52.701
-Yes. Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.701 --> 00:04:56.667
-And yet he seems very surprised
and delighted

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:58.133
by the quality of the floors.

00:04:58.133 --> 00:04:59.634
Were they great-looking floors?

00:04:59.634 --> 00:05:00.968
-No, they really weren't.
-Really? Okay.

00:05:00.968 --> 00:05:02.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:04.567
-I mean, Mar-a-Lago is actually
very beautiful.

00:05:04.567 --> 00:05:05.968
And the room that we were in was

00:05:05.968 --> 00:05:07.901
actually a really beautiful room
as well.

00:05:07.901 --> 00:05:09.868
-It does genuinely look
beautiful on film. Yeah.

00:05:09.868 --> 00:05:12.801
-But, I mean, the least most
beautiful thing

00:05:12.801 --> 00:05:14.634
in the entire room
was the floor.

00:05:14.634 --> 00:05:17.534
So, he walks in, I go,
"Hello, Mr. President."

00:05:17.534 --> 00:05:20.701
And he completely ignores me and
then goes, "Look at this floor."

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:22.133
And I'm like, "What?"

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:24.901
Of all the things to look at,
I mean, there's this, like,

00:05:24.901 --> 00:05:27.434
hideous painting of him from
like 30 years ago behind

00:05:27.434 --> 00:05:29.467
that's like an oil painting,
which was, like,

00:05:29.467 --> 00:05:31.267
the most eye-catching of
everything in there.

00:05:31.267 --> 00:05:33.434
But, like, literally, the floor
of all the things.

00:05:33.434 --> 00:05:36.100
Then he comes in, sits down,
and then we start having

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.801
a conversation about the last
time I'd interviewed him,

00:05:38.801 --> 00:05:42.033
he was in the White House.
And he says, "Yeah, but this is

00:05:42.033 --> 00:05:43.634
much nicer than the White House,
isn't it?"

00:05:43.634 --> 00:05:45.234
I mean, that's the thing with
Trump -- everything that

00:05:45.234 --> 00:05:47.701
he owns, everything that he
touches, everything that's got

00:05:47.701 --> 00:05:50.367
his name on it is definitely
better than anything else.

00:05:50.367 --> 00:05:51.968
-Yeah. Well you haven't lived
here as long,

00:05:51.968 --> 00:05:53.801
but you might not know,
he's mentally ill.

00:05:53.801 --> 00:05:55.367
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:55.367 --> 00:05:57.667
So that's -- that's what it is.

00:05:57.667 --> 00:05:59.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:59.934 --> 00:06:05.033
So, wait, you -- I do want to
say, I know that you went on

00:06:05.033 --> 00:06:08.567
this journey where you thought
that he was lying about the fact

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:11.667
that he won the election,
but over the course of

00:06:11.667 --> 00:06:13.934
these interviews, you've
actually come to believe

00:06:13.934 --> 00:06:17.267
that he does believe that he had
this election stolen from him.

00:06:17.267 --> 00:06:19.000
-He's bat[bleep] crazy, the guy.
I mean, there's no question.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.400
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.067
-But this was a journey
you took, right?

00:06:22.067 --> 00:06:24.300
-Absolutely. I mean, the idea
that I would have had

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:28.567
a preconceived notion that he
really believed in his own lie

00:06:28.567 --> 00:06:31.901
before I met him was something
that just is beyond

00:06:31.901 --> 00:06:33.334
anything I could have
comprehended. Right?

00:06:33.334 --> 00:06:35.267
I mean, this is the President of
the United States of America.

00:06:35.267 --> 00:06:36.734
And when I interviewed him
for the first time,

00:06:36.734 --> 00:06:37.868
you know,
he's in the White House,

00:06:37.868 --> 00:06:40.000
all the apparatus of
the presidency is there.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.501
The guy with
the nuclear football

00:06:41.501 --> 00:06:43.167
is outside the room, right?

00:06:43.167 --> 00:06:44.501
Secret Service is everywhere.

00:06:44.501 --> 00:06:46.934
You know, "Mogul on the move."
That's his code name.

00:06:46.934 --> 00:06:48.300
I mean,
it's all completely insane.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:49.968
And he's looking me in the eye,
and he's telling me --

00:06:49.968 --> 00:06:52.234
this is after his own
attorney general had said

00:06:52.234 --> 00:06:54.200
there was no basis whatsoever

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:56.067
for any of the election
conspiracies that he was

00:06:56.067 --> 00:06:58.334
still going on about
and still does go on about.

00:06:58.334 --> 00:07:00.434
And so, he's looking me in
the eye, and he's telling me,

00:07:00.434 --> 00:07:02.634
"There's no way Biden got
80 million votes

00:07:02.634 --> 00:07:05.868
and we need to reopen all
the ballots in Georgia

00:07:05.868 --> 00:07:08.200
to find these extra votes."

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:12.267
So, I mean, it was just crazy
because at the end of the day,

00:07:12.267 --> 00:07:14.734
if the President of the United
States has come to believe in

00:07:14.734 --> 00:07:18.501
his own lie, that's really scary
and terrifying.

00:07:18.501 --> 00:07:21.767
And so I remember, like, after
he left, I sort of put my hand

00:07:21.767 --> 00:07:23.534
on the wall, and I was like,

00:07:23.534 --> 00:07:25.167
"Actually, I'm not going to
think about this now.

00:07:25.167 --> 00:07:26.300
I'll wait until I get back to
the hotel"

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:28.868
'cause it was just too insane.
But yeah.

00:07:28.868 --> 00:07:31.367
-I wonder how many times someone
has had, you know,

00:07:31.367 --> 00:07:34.200
a private moment with the
president and then just

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:36.000
walked out and put their hand
on the wall...

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:37.834
[ Laughter ]
...and just, like, taking

00:07:37.834 --> 00:07:40.267
a moment before going on with
the rest of their day.

00:07:40.267 --> 00:07:42.767
I really, truly hope
you don't have to

00:07:42.767 --> 00:07:45.434
make a sequel to this series.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:45.434 --> 00:07:47.601
But I'm so glad you made
the first one. Thank you so much

00:07:47.601 --> 00:07:49.334
for being here. It's really
a delight talking to you.

00:07:49.334 --> 00:07:50.501
Alex Holder, everybody.

00:07:50.501 --> 00:07:53.267
"Unprecedented" is streaming
on Discovery+.

00:07:53.267 --> 00:07:57.133
We'll be right back with comedy
from Hoodo Hersi.

